From 691f1a5bbad5f936e79c8a08d69239e6840ac40f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 02:01:01 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07009/11362] Wire score_goal_predicate_consistency into a live
 veto (REQ-ARC-WMTE-5593-3)

Closes the gap REQ-ARC-WMTE-5593 explicitly left open: the goal-hypothesis
consistency check was built and unit-tested but never consulted by any live
decision. Its own docstring names the exact target: execute_bounded_llm_
reinduction "installs outcome.goal_predicate as a search termination
condition on the strength of the proposer's own code, unchecked against any
observed transition."

Prerequisite bug found and fixed first: score_goal_predicate_consistency's
core logic (real_levelup = level_after > level_before) needs correct
Transition.level_before, but E3AgentPolicy's live Transition-construction
sites (next_move, _remember_active_probe_origin) hardcoded level_before=0
unconditionally. Wiring the check against raw live transitions without this
fix would have judged every predicate against systematically wrong ground
truth past the first level-up. Fixed by adding self._prev_level, captured
alongside every self._prev assignment (mirroring AutonomousExplorer._ingest's
own previous_best_level pattern), consumed as level_before instead of the
hardcoded 0. Verified via a ~280-test regression sweep across every
E3AgentPolicy-touching test file (one pre-existing unrelated registry-drift
failure confirmed present before this change too: test_experiment_5176's
hardcoded cd82 snapshot vs. the registry's real, legitimately-advanced
depth). Also fixed a stale test from the earlier induce_prompt scalability
commit (test_experiment_4664's WIN STATE assertion still expected the old
raw to_ascii format instead of _rle_grid's row-wise encoding) -- caught by
this same regression sweep, landed via an intervening conductor checkpoint
commit (ed9b0b71f) rather than this one, noted here for provenance.

Safety precondition confirmed BEFORE wiring anything: is_level_complete is
used ONLY as plan_in_model's in-model BFS terminal condition -- a pure
simulation-internal search hint. The live agent's REAL win-recognition
(E3AgentPolicy._current_goal_reached, comparing explorer.best_level against
the real environment's own level signal) is entirely independent of the
induced predicate. A veto is therefore low-risk: worst case, plan_in_model
finds no plan that round and the phase machine falls back to real
exploration -- actual level-progress detection is untouched either way.

Design mirrors the EXISTING dynamics-veto pattern rather than inventing a
new one: a new min_goal_predicate_consistency=0.0 (default off) parameter;
when set, right after goal satisfiability is confirmed and BEFORE
plan_in_model runs, score the predicate against the same transitions the
dynamics check already uses. Vetoes ONLY when accuracy is below threshold
AND n_real_levelups>=1 (CLAUDE.md FALSE_NEGATIVE_RISK discipline -- an
all-no-op window makes any predicate, including a constant-False stub,
trivially score 1.0, so judging on that data would be uninformative). On
veto: attach a goal_predicate_consistency_failed counterexample, skip the
round, continue to refactor() via the existing generic fallback path (not
the dynamics-specific BEFORE/PREDICTED/OBSERVED shape, since a goal
mismatch isn't a grid-prediction mismatch).

Live call site now passes min_goal_predicate_consistency=1.0 -- mirroring
that SAME call's own existing min_heldout_accuracy=1.0, the established
risk tolerance for this gate. Genuinely live, not inert plumbing: a bad
goal predicate found during live re-induction now gets rejected and
triggers a refactor attempt instead of being installed unchecked.

4 new tests (veto fires on a real mismatch, opt-in/disabled-by-default
backward compatibility, false-negative-risk guard). REQ-ARC-WMTE-5593-3 +
3 SCENARIOs added to spec.md.

